clients: never define BONDING_SUPPORT against mainline bonding

The three sub-Makefiles that build against a bond device gate -DBONDING_SUPPORT
on the kernel's own CONFIG_BONDING:

    ifneq (,$(filter $(CONFIG_BONDING),y m))
    ccflags-y += -DBONDING_SUPPORT

but what the define guards is not "the kernel has bonding" - it is "the kernel
has QSDK's *patched* bonding". nss_connmgr_pppoe.c calls bond_get_id(), and the
bridge/vlan managers use struct bond_cb; mainline's bonding driver exports
neither. So on this tree the test is asking the wrong question, and when it
answers yes the build stops:

  nss_connmgr_pppoe.c:290:26: error: implicit declaration of function
      'bond_get_id'; did you mean 'find_get_pid'? [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]

Nothing noticed until KMODS=1, because CONFIG_BONDING was simply never set:
build.sh already strips the +kmod-bonding dependency qca-nss-drv-pppoe declares
(QSDK boilerplate for LAG over PPPoE), and nothing else pulled bonding in.
ALL_KMODS selects every module, CONFIG_BONDING becomes m, and the define
appears - in kmod-qca-nss-drv-pppoe, which is in DEVICE_PACKAGES, so the whole
NSS build fails.

Point the test at a symbol that does not exist rather than deleting the block,
so it is obvious what the condition was and what would have to be true to
restore it.

No behaviour change for this port: with BONDING_SUPPORT undefined, PPPoE over a
bond master leaves bondid at -1 and the connection is refused - which is what
already happened here, since the module was always built without the define.
LAG is not part of this board's topology.

--- a/pppoe/Makefile
+++ b/pppoe/Makefile
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@
 obj-m += qca-nss-pppoe.o
 qca-nss-pppoe-objs := nss_connmgr_pppoe.o
 
-ifneq (,$(filter $(CONFIG_BONDING),y m))
+# BONDING_SUPPORT gates calls into QSDK's patched bonding driver -
+# bond_get_id() here, struct bond_cb elsewhere. Mainline bonding has neither,
+# so the define is wrong on this tree whatever CONFIG_BONDING says.
+ifneq (,$(filter $(CONFIG_BONDING_QSDK_PATCHED),y m))
 ccflags-y += -DBONDING_SUPPORT
 endif
--- a/bridge/Makefile
+++ b/bridge/Makefile
@@ -15,6 +15,9 @@
